Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,A man sits in a dark\Nroom in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.94,0:00:03.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,front of a black\Nscreen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.91,0:00:06.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,The red words tell him\Nhis wife
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.32,0:00:08.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,is already dead\Ndownstairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.87,0:00:11.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,They say the man who\Ndid it is still in the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.96,0:00:15.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,house, coming up the\Nstairs for him now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.28,0:00:16.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,Jack does not run.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.97,0:00:19.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,He is crying, and he\Nis about to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.14,0:00:21.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,thank the thing on the\Nscreen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.47,0:00:23.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let us go back to the\Nbeginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.69,0:00:26.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,Twelve years earlier,\NJack had
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.15,0:00:28.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,a cheap flat and a\Ntired job.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.84,0:00:31.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,One night his screen\Nwent black, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.77,0:00:35.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,red letters asked him\Nfor a favour.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.07,0:00:38.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,In his office lobby\Nthere was a plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.17,0:00:40.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,Move it three inches\Nto the left.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.61,0:00:42.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,Nothing wrong, nothing\Nagainst
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.01,0:00:45.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,the law, nobody hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.14,0:00:48.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,So he did it, and he\Nforgot about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.20,0:00:50.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,Three days later a\Nwoman stopped to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.99,0:00:53.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,push that plant\Nstraight, and was
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.62,0:00:56.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,still there when the\Nlift opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.70,0:00:58.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,That is how Jack met\NAllie.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.67,0:01:01.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two cubicles away for\Na year, and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.22,0:01:04.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,he had never spoken to\Nher once.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.15,0:01:05.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,He asked what it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.97,0:01:07.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,It said it was a seer.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.63,0:01:10.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,It could see every\Npossible thing that
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.42,0:01:13.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,could happen, and\Nevery road to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.44,0:01:16.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,It had done this for\Nthousands of years,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.57,0:01:19.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,and always took the\Nsame payment.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.45,0:01:21.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,One favour, then the\Nnext.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.84,0:01:25.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,A lorry missed Allie\Nby two seconds because
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.21,0:01:28.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,Jack made a phone ring\Nat a junction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.40,0:01:30.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,A stranger won twenty\Nseven million
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.99,0:01:33.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,because Jack stood in\Na queue.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.66,0:01:36.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,The screen was not\Ngiving him luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.31,0:01:38.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was spending other\Npeople
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.29,0:01:40.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,to build the life he\Nwanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.71,0:01:42.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,He married Donna.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.14,0:01:43.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,He bought the big\Nhouse at
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.77,0:01:45.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,the end of the long\Nroad.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.63,0:01:48.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,Twelve good years,\Npaid for by
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.11,0:01:50.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,favours he never\Nquestioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.87,0:01:53.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then came the\Ndoorbell, a delivery
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.83,0:01:55.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,boy with a warm box,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.58,0:01:57.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,and a wife on the sofa\Nwho
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.85,0:02:00.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,would not wake up\Nagain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.39,0:02:02.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,Upstairs the red\Nletters
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.18,0:02:03.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,told him the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.90,0:02:06.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,The boy had been a\Nfavour too.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.02,0:02:08.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Years before, Jack had\Nheld a
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.22,0:02:10.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,door for a frightened\Nchild.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.80,0:02:13.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,It said it had been\Npainting one
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.46,0:02:16.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,picture for a very\Nlong time, that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.29,0:02:18.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Jack was one brush\Nstroke in
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.62,0:02:21.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,it, and it was nearly\Nfinished.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.65,0:02:25.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the doorway stood a\Nlarge shape, breathing
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.28,0:02:27.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,hard, with a knife\Nheld low.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.83,0:02:31.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,The screen asked if he\Nhad nothing to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.16,0:02:34.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,And Jack, who had been\Ngiven twelve
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.02,0:02:36.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,good years for a plant\Nmoved
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.30,0:02:38.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,three inches, said the\Ntwo
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.43,0:02:40.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,words he had been\Npromised.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.93,0:02:42.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.16,0:02:45.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is my retelling\Nof The Seer
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.14,0:02:47.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,of Possibilities, by\NThomas
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.66,0:02:50.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,O., on creepypasta dot\Ncom.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.63,0:02:52.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Would you have done\Nthe first favour?
